# ⚠️ DO NOT deploy this file by overwriting public_html/.htaccess wholesale
# — that file already contains cPanel-auto-generated PHP directives (error
# logging, PHP version handler) marked "do not edit," regenerated by
# cPanel's own MultiPHP INI Editor. This repo copy exists for version
# history/reference only. To actually apply this on the server: open
# public_html/.htaccess in cPanel File Manager's Edit view (Show Hidden
# Files must be on) and APPEND just the block below to the end of the
# existing file — never replace the whole file. (The HTTPS redirect from
# cPanel's Force HTTPS Redirect toggle does NOT live in this file, despite
# first appearances — it's handled server/vhost-side, outside public_html
# entirely — so nothing needs adding here for that.)

# Force browsers to revalidate JS/CSS on every visit instead of serving a
# possibly-stale cached copy indefinitely. This site is deployed manually
# (no cache-busting version query strings on script/link tags across 49
# pages), and stale browser caches repeatedly made real, already-deployed
# fixes look like they hadn't shipped — confirmed more than once by testing
# the same URLs in a private/incognito window, which always showed the
# correct, current content. `no-cache` still allows caching, it just forces
# a conditional request (If-Modified-Since/ETag) before reusing the cached
# copy, so a real change is picked up on the very next visit rather than
# only after the cache naturally expires or the user manually clears it.
<IfModule mod_headers.c>
  <FilesMatch "\.(js|css)$">
    Header set Cache-Control "no-cache, must-revalidate"
  </FilesMatch>
</IfModule>
